Writing to 'fraction_done' inside a tight computation loop may introduce significant I/O overhead. Consider reducing the frequency of file writes, for example by updating the file at fixed intervals.
```suggestion
    double last_update_time = 0.0; // Track the last update time
    while (1) {
        double t = clock()/(double)CLOCKS_PER_SEC;
        if (t >= nsecs) break;
        do_a_giga_flop(i++);
        if (t - last_update_time >= 1.0) { // Update every 1 second
            FILE *f = fopen("fraction_done", "w");
            fprintf(f, "%f\n", t/nsecs);
            fclose(f);
            last_update_time = t; // Update the last update time
        }
```

