`fd` is only set when `!seg_ptr`; on subsequent calls it remains `0`, so `fstat(fd, ...)` targets stdin rather than the shm object. Also, `mmap()` failure returns `MAP_FAILED` (non-null), so `if (!seg_ptr)` won’t catch failures, and `shm_open()` failure (`-1`) is not handled before calling `mmap()`. Restructure initialization to: open shm, validate `fd`, `fstat()` size check, then `mmap()` and verify `seg_ptr != MAP_FAILED`; close `fd` once mapping succeeds (or store `fd` alongside `seg_ptr` if you truly need it later).
