`parse_next_element()` cursor advancement and element detection are currently unsafe: it uses `strlen($element)` even when `$element` is null (TypeError in PHP 8+), uses `if ($n)` which misses empty elements, and advances `$cursor` based on `strlen($xml) - strlen($x)` even though `$x` comes from `$pos = substr($xml, $cursor)` (so the computed offset is wrong). Also `if (!$element)` treats the string "0" as missing. Consider switching to `strpos($xml, $tag, $cursor)` to get an absolute position, using `!== false` checks, only advancing the cursor when a match is found, and distinguishing `null` from valid-but-falsy strings.
```suggestion
